<title>USA: Neotherapeutics to begin clinical trials.</title>
<headline>Neotherapeutics to begin clinical trials.</headline>
<dateline>IRVINE, Calif. 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>NeoTherapeutics Inc said Friday it received clearance from the Food and Drug Administration to begin Phase I clinical trials of its AIT-082 compound for Alzheimer's disease.</p>
<p>AIT-082 is a small molecule designed to cross the blood-brain barrier. It has been shown in preclinical studies to enhance cognitive function and memory in animals with neurological deficits.</p>
